From: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 23:23:18 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] squashfs-sanity-check-directory-metadata-block-location-fix

squashfs_lookup() stores squashfs_dir_start() in a u64 then checks block <
0.  That check cannot detect its negative error returns; block needs a
signed type.

Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Cc: Phillip Lougher <phillip.lougher@gmail.com>
Cc: Phillip Lougher <phillip@squashfs.org.uk>

 fs/squashfs/namei.c |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)
---
 fs/squashfs/namei.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/fs/squashfs/namei.c b/fs/squashfs/namei.c
index 9f6f6792b5498..09bd0075dd84f 100644
--- a/fs/squashfs/namei.c
+++ b/fs/squashfs/namei.c
@@ -138,7 +138,7 @@ static struct dentry *squashfs_lookup(struct inode *dir, struct dentry *dentry,
 
 	TRACE("Entered squashfs_lookup [%llx:%x]\n", squashfs_i(dir)->start, offset);
 
-	if (block < 0)
+	if ((s64)block < 0)
 		goto data_error;
 
 	dire = kmalloc(sizeof(*dire) + SQUASHFS_NAME_LEN + 1, GFP_KERNEL);
-- 
2.47.3

